# Milestone: M3 (activated v0.14.0-refoundation)
# Covers: two watchers whose conditions become true at the same moment
#         fire in REGISTRATION order.  Both bodies append their own letter
#         to one accumulator, so "AB" is the whole claim: a sum or a
#         counter could not tell the two orders apart.
#
#         Both conditions are `true`, so they hold at install and the
#         first drain fires both -- which is the simultaneity the fixture
#         wants, without a clock.
#
#         Previously a placeholder claiming the `at` body's fork path was
#         unavailable through the runner.  It is available: watcher bodies
#         are spawned as scheduled strands, and a drain runs after every
#         slice, so by the time the installing chunk returns both have
#         run.
# matrix-row: scheduler-fifo

## mode: file

var log = "";
at (true) { log = log + "A" };
at (true) { log = log + "B" };
echo(log)
[00000000] *** AB
